1,0$ Key 2 : Veil leaving flocks adhering to pileus margin, occasionally also on stipe. Cheilocystidia subcylindrical, lageniform, sublecythiform or utriform. (sect.Vestitae and Intermediae) 
1,0,n$ N.B.The flocks of the veil in this group are thin, fibrillose, andneversulcate-striate.The yareloosely attached to the pileus surface and may be easily washedoffbyrain. Therefore, they are often lacking in older basidiocarps. Such basidiocarps may be identified with key four. See also remarks under key one.
